# Geometry

Areas, perimeters, volumes and surface areas of the standard shapes, coordinate formulas, the conic sections and polygon angles. Import with `![[std/geometry.mpp]]`, or one formula with `Using $A_{\text{circle}}$ from [[std/geometry.mpp]].`

## Plane figures

The area of a circle of radius $r$.

$$ A_{\text{circle}}(r) := \pi r^2 $$

$$ A_{\text{circle}}(3) \overset{?}{=} 9\pi $$

The circumference of a circle of radius $r$.

$$ C_{\text{circle}}(r) := 2 \pi r $$

$$ C_{\text{circle}}(\tfrac{1}{2}) \overset{?}{=} \pi $$

The area of a rectangle and of a triangle with base $b$ and height $h$.

$$ A_{\text{rect}}(a, b) := a b $$

$$ A_{\text{rect}}(3, 4) \overset{?}{=} 12 $$

$$ A_{\text{triangle}}(b, h) := \frac{1}{2} b h $$

$$ A_{\text{triangle}}(6, 4) \overset{?}{=} 12 $$

The area of a trapezium with parallel sides $a$, $b$ and height $h$.

$$ A_{\text{trap}}(a, b, h) := \frac{(a + b) h}{2} $$

$$ A_{\text{trap}}(3, 5, 2) \overset{?}{=} 8 $$

The area of a sector of angle $\theta$ and the length of its arc.

$$ A_{\text{sector}}(r, \theta) := \frac{1}{2} r^2 \theta $$

$$ A_{\text{sector}}(2, \tfrac{\pi}{2}) \overset{?}{=} \pi $$

$$ s_{\text{arc}}(r, \theta) := r \theta $$

$$ s_{\text{arc}}(3, \tfrac{\pi}{3}) \overset{?}{=} \pi $$

The area of an ellipse with semi-axes $a$ and $b$.

$$ A_{\text{ellipse}}(a, b) := \pi a b $$

$$ A_{\text{ellipse}}(2, 3) \overset{?}{=} 6\pi $$

The area and perimeter of a regular $n$-gon with side $s$.

$$ A_{\text{ngon}}(n, s) := \frac{n s^2}{4 \tan(\pi / n)} $$

$$ A_{\text{ngon}}(4, 3) \overset{?}{=} 9 $$

$$ A_{\text{ngon}}(6, 2) \overset{?}{=} 6\sqrt{3} $$

## Solids

The volume and surface area of a ball of radius $r$.

$$ V_{\text{ball}}(r) := \frac{4}{3} \pi r^3 $$

$$ V_{\text{ball}}(3) \overset{?}{=} 36\pi $$

$$ S_{\text{sphere}}(r) := 4 \pi r^2 $$

$$ S_{\text{sphere}}(\tfrac{1}{2}) \overset{?}{=} \pi $$

The surface area is the derivative of the volume with respect to the radius.

$$ \frac{d}{dr} V_{\text{ball}}(r) \overset{?}{=} S_{\text{sphere}}(r) $$

$$ \int_{-r}^{r} \pi (r^2 - x^2) \, dx \overset{?}{=} V_{\text{ball}}(r) $$

A cylinder of radius $r$ and height $h$.

$$ V_{\text{cyl}}(r, h) := \pi r^2 h $$

$$ V_{\text{cyl}}(2, 5) \overset{?}{=} 20\pi $$

$$ S_{\text{cyl}}(r, h) := 2\pi r^2 + 2\pi r h $$

$$ S_{\text{cyl}}(1, 1) \overset{?}{=} 4\pi $$

A cone of radius $r$ and height $h$; its surface includes the base.

$$ V_{\text{cone}}(r, h) := \frac{1}{3} \pi r^2 h $$

$$ V_{\text{cone}}(3, 4) \overset{?}{=} 12\pi $$

$$ S_{\text{cone}}(r, h) := \pi r^2 + \pi r \sqrt{r^2 + h^2} $$

$$ S_{\text{cone}}(3, 4) \overset{?}{=} 24\pi $$

A box with edges $a$, $b$, $c$, and a pyramid with base area $B$ and height $h$.

$$ V_{\text{box}}(a, b, c) := a b c $$

$$ V_{\text{box}}(2, 3, 4) \overset{?}{=} 24 $$

$$ S_{\text{box}}(a, b, c) := 2(ab + bc + ca) $$

$$ S_{\text{box}}(2, 3, 4) \overset{?}{=} 52 $$

$$ V_{\text{pyramid}}(B, h) := \frac{1}{3} B h $$

$$ V_{\text{pyramid}}(9, 4) \overset{?}{=} 12 $$

A torus with tube radius $r$ around a circle of radius $R$.

$$ V_{\text{torus}}(R, r) := 2\pi^2 R r^2 $$

$$ V_{\text{torus}}(2, 1) \overset{?}{=} 4\pi^2 $$

## Coordinates

The distance between $(x_1, y_1)$ and $(x_2, y_2)$.

$$ d_{\text{2D}}(x_1, y_1, x_2, y_2) := \sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2} $$

$$ d_{\text{2D}}(0, 0, 3, 4) \overset{?}{=} 5 $$

The distance in space.

$$ d_{\text{3D}}(x_1, y_1, z_1, x_2, y_2, z_2) := \sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2 + (z_2 - z_1)^2} $$

$$ d_{\text{3D}}(1, 2, 3, 3, 4, 4) \overset{?}{=} 3 $$

The midpoint of a segment, one coordinate at a time.

$$ m_{\text{mid}}(a, b) := \frac{a + b}{2} $$

$$ m_{\text{mid}}(2, 8) \overset{?}{=} 5 $$

The section formula: the point dividing the segment from $a$ to $b$ in the ratio $m : n$.

$$ p_{\text{section}}(a, b, m, n) := \frac{n a + m b}{m + n} $$

$$ p_{\text{section}}(0, 10, 2, 3) \overset{?}{=} 4 $$

The slope of the line through two points, and the distance from $(x_0, y_0)$ to the line $a x + b y + c = 0$.

$$ m_{\text{slope}}(x_1, y_1, x_2, y_2) := \frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} $$

$$ m_{\text{slope}}(1, 2, 3, 8) \overset{?}{=} 3 $$

$$ d_{\text{line}}(a, b, c, x_0, y_0) := \frac{|a x_0 + b y_0 + c|}{\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}} $$

$$ d_{\text{line}}(3, 4, -10, 0, 0) \overset{?}{=} 2 $$

## Conic sections

Each curve is written as a function that is zero exactly on the curve.

A circle of radius $r$ centred at $(h, k)$.

$$ Q_{\text{circle}}(x, y, h, k, r) := (x - h)^2 + (y - k)^2 - r^2 $$

$$ Q_{\text{circle}}(4, 6, 1, 2, 5) \overset{?}{=} 0 $$

An ellipse with semi-axes $a$ and $b$, centred at the origin, and its eccentricity.

$$ Q_{\text{ellipse}}(x, y, a, b) := \frac{x^2}{a^2} + \frac{y^2}{b^2} - 1 $$

$$ Q_{\text{ellipse}}(a \cos t, b \sin t, a, b) \overset{?}{=} 0 $$

$$ e_{\text{ellipse}}(a, b) := \sqrt{1 - \frac{b^2}{a^2}} $$

$$ e_{\text{ellipse}}(5, 3) \overset{?}{=} \frac{4}{5} $$

A parabola with focus $(0, p)$ and directrix $y = -p$.

$$ Q_{\text{parabola}}(x, y, p) := x^2 - 4 p y $$

$$ Q_{\text{parabola}}(4, 2, 2) \overset{?}{=} 0 $$

A hyperbola with semi-axes $a$ and $b$, and its asymptote slopes $\pm b/a$.

$$ Q_{\text{hyperbola}}(x, y, a, b) := \frac{x^2}{a^2} - \frac{y^2}{b^2} - 1 $$

$$ Q_{\text{hyperbola}}(a \cosh t, b \sinh t, a, b) \overset{?}{=} 0 $$

## Polygon angles

The sum of the interior angles of an $n$-gon, and each interior angle of a regular one, in degrees.

$$ \Sigma_{\text{interior}}(n) := 180 (n - 2) $$

$$ \Sigma_{\text{interior}}(6) \overset{?}{=} 720 $$

$$ \theta_{\text{interior}}(n) := \frac{180 (n - 2)}{n} $$

$$ \theta_{\text{interior}}(5) \overset{?}{=} 108 $$

The exterior angles of any convex polygon add to $360^\circ$.

$$ n (180 - \theta_{\text{interior}}(n)) \overset{?}{=} 360 $$

## Pythagoras

**Theorem.** (Pythagoras) In a right triangle with legs $a$, $b$ and hypotenuse $c$, $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$.

$$ 3^2 + 4^2 \overset{?}{=} 5^2 $$

$$ 5^2 + 12^2 \overset{?}{=} 13^2 $$
